# An image built from this work tree sees what a fresh checkout would, because
# that is what CI builds the published image from. Without this file a local
# build - task image, task stage - sent everything git keeps out of the
# repository, and what lies in cmd/configs is copied into the image: measured, a
# datasource.json left there by the installer put its password in a layer, and
# the image skipped its installer and connected to the database it named.
#
# So this is .gitignore, line by line and in its order, written the way Docker
# reads a pattern: from the root of the context, where git matches a name with no
# slash at any depth. Add to .gitignore, not here first;
# test/dockerignore_test.go says what this file has to say then.

# The repository itself: most of what a build sent, and changed by every commit.
.git

**/bin
**/coverage.out

**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal

configs/datasource.json
cmd/configs/datasource.json
bin/configs/datasource.json

deploy/.env
deploy/.env.ci

cmd/configs/.local.env
bin/configs/.local.env

**/dist
**/*.syso
build/versioninfo.json
test/browser/*.png
**/AUDIT_REPORT.md

.gotmp/*
!.gotmp/.gitkeep
